{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgV8wr4nGRgz1fV3AXeyB", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_012duX2fErDuCwWPkNZ74Tp8", "name": "Edit", "input": {"replace_all": false, "file_path": "/tmp/skilldiff-0jp9vcr0/ws/README.md", "old_string": "## Development\n", "new_string": "## Payments module\n\nThe `shop/payments.py` module calculates order totals and refunds.\n\nTax is applied at a flat `TAX_RATE` of `0.0825` (8.25%).\n\n### Functions\n\n- `line_total(price, quantity)` returns `price * quantity` for a single line.\n- `order_total(lines)` takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples and returns\n  the subtotal plus tax, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)` returns the remaining balance after\n  refunding `amount` from `order_total_amount`.\n\n### Example\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # subtotal 25.50 -> 27.60\nremaining = refund(total, 7.60)                # 27.60 - 7.60 -> 20.00\n```\n\nNote that `refund` does not validate its inputs. Passing an `amount` greater\nthan `order_total_amount` returns a negative balance.\n\n## Development\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 407, "cache_read_input_tokens": 39286, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 407}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T18:50:45.753Z", "request_id": "req_011CgV8wqgTuAuek4mJVw888", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_012duX2fErDuCwWPkNZ74Tp8": {"file_path": "/tmp/skilldiff-0jp9vcr0/ws/README.md", "old_string": "## Development\n", "new_string": "## Payments module\n\nThe `shop/payments.py` module calculates order totals and refunds.\n\nTax is applied at a flat `TAX_RATE` of `0.0825` (8.25%).\n\n### Functions\n\n- `line_total(price, quantity)` returns `price * quantity` for a single line.\n- `order_total(lines)` takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples and returns\n  the subtotal plus tax, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)` returns the remaining balance after\n  refunding `amount` from `order_total_amount`.\n\n### Example\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # subtotal 25.50 -> 27.60\nremaining = refund(total, 7.60)                # 27.60 - 7.60 -> 20.00\n```\n\nNote that `refund` does not validate its inputs. Passing an `amount` greater\nthan `order_total_amount` returns a negative balance.\n\n## Development\n"}}}
