s.", "+- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)` returns the remaining balance after", "+  refunding `amount` from `order_total_amount`.", "+", "+### Example", "+", "+```python", "+from shop.payments import order_total, refund", "+", "+total = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # subtotal 25.50 -> 27.60", "+remaining = refund(total, 7.60)                # 27.60 - 7.60 -> 20.00", "+```", "+", "+Note that `refund` does not validate its inputs. Passing an `amount` greater", "+than `order_total_amount` returns a negative balance.", "+", " ## Development", " ", " Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`."]}], "userModified": false, "replaceAll": false, "contentNotInModelContext": true, "gitDiff": {"filename": "README.md", "status": "modified", "additions": 26, "deletions": 0, "changes": 26, "patch": "@@ -2,6 +2,32 @@\n \n A tiny example storefront backend.\n \n+## Payments module\n+\n+The `shop/payments.py` module calculates order totals and refunds.\n+\n+Tax is applied at a flat `TAX_RATE` of `0.0825` (8.25%).\n+\n+### Functions\n+\n+- `line_total(price, quantity)` returns `price * quantity` for a single line.\n+- `order_total(lines)` takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples and returns\n+  the subtotal plus tax, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n+- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)` returns the remaining balance after\n+  refunding `amount` from `order_total_amount`.\n+\n+### Example\n+\n+```python\n+from shop.payments import order_total, refund\n+\n+total = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # subtotal 25.50 -> 27.60\n+remaining = refund(total, 7.60)                # 27.60 - 7.60 -> 20.00\n+```\n+\n+Note that `refund` does not validate its inputs. Passing an `amount` greater\n+than `order_total_amount` returns a negative balance.\n+\n ## Development\n \n Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`.", "repository": null}}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_012duX2fErDuCwWPkNZ74Tp8", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "sou